Q: TOP keyword in sql is not working A: <p>Equivalent query in <code>mysql</code>.Use <code>LIMIT</code>.<code>TOP</code> is used in <code>SQL Server / MS Access</code>.</p>

<pre><code>SELECT salary FROM salary ORDER BY SALARY DESC LIMIT 3;
</code></pre>

Q: In mysql workbench &#39;select top&#39; is not working... how can i access top 5 in table? A: <pre><code>    SELECT TOP &lt;Number&gt; &lt;column_name(s)&gt; 
    FROM &lt;table_name&gt; 
    WHERE &lt;condition&gt;; 
</code></pre>
<p>For this SQL query corresponding MYSQL query is</p>
<pre><code>    SELECT &lt;column_name(s)&gt; 
    FROM &lt;table_name&gt; 
    WHERE &lt;condition&gt;
    LIMIT number;
</code></pre>
<p>Using TOP will give the error.</p>

Q: UncategorizedMongoDbException: Command failed with error 10107 (NotMaster): &#39;not master&#39; on server A: <p>It happens the same to me because the container was not fully started.</p>
<p>You might consider using <code>Startables.deepStart(mongoDBContainer).join()</code></p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>@ExtendWith(SpringExtension.class)
@Testcontainers
class MongoConnectionTest {
  @Container
  static MongoDBContainer mongoDBContainer = new MongoDBContainer(DockerImageName.parse(&quot;mongo:4.1.3&quot;));


  @DynamicPropertySource
  static void dynamicPropertySource(DynamicPropertyRegistry registry) {
    Startables.deepStart(mongoDBContainer).join(); //wait for containers to start
    //...
  }

  @Test
  void shouldSaveAnEntity() {
    //Given
    ConnectionString cs = new ConnectionString(mongoDBContainer.getReplicaSetUrl());
    MongoClient mongoClient = MongoClients.create(cs);
    ReactiveMongoTemplate mongoTemplate = new ReactiveMongoTemplate(mongoClient, &quot;test&quot;);

    //When
    Mono&lt;Entity&gt; steps = mongoTemplate.save(new Entity(&quot;id&quot;, &quot;name&quot;, &quot;description&quot;))
        .then(mongoTemplate.findOne(Query.query(Criteria.where(&quot;id&quot;).is(&quot;id&quot;)), Entity.class));

    //Then
    StepVerifier.create(steps).assertNext(e -&gt; {
      Assertions.assertThat(e.id()).isEqualTo(&quot;id&quot;);
    }).verifyComplete();
  }
}

record Entity(@Id String id, String name, String description) {

}
</code></pre>

